  "notes": "First formal evidence-based baseline for an entity with no prior assessment. Filed on both the magnitude trigger (delta -13.2) and the band-crossing trigger (Functional to Developing). ALLEGATION DISCIPLINE (Netflix precedent, which the cycle brief specifically required): neither the 14 September 2026 Khalil/SIPA suit nor the August 2026 Palestinian students and faculty suit is scored as a finding, and the allegation that Columbia retained private investigators is not scored at all. Every score-moving fact is a completed act, a regulator finding or a published agreement — principally the 2025-05-23 joint HHS/Department of Education Title VI Notice of Violation, the 2025-07-23 Federal Resolution Agreement Columbia publishes itself, the EEOC 21 million dollar settlement now in payout, and the 2026-02-27 StandWithUs settlement. The assessment would reach the same band if both pending suits were dismissed. The September suit appears at AB4 only as evidence that the pattern of claims recurs, which bears on documented systemic learning rather than on the merits of the new claim. NOTE ON PRIMARY SOURCES: hhs.gov, ed.gov and axios.com all returned HTTP 403 to automated retrieval, so no verbatim quote is attached to the federal finding; it is captured as a claim against the agencies’ own URLs per the evidence-integrity rule.",
